<title>UK: EUROMARKET TURNOVER FELL IN WEEK TO 7 AUGUST -ISMA.</title>
<headline>EUROMARKET TURNOVER FELL IN WEEK TO 7 AUGUST -ISMA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turnover in the Eurobond and related markets fell to $1.034 trillion in the week to August 7 from $1.123 trillion in the previous week, International Securities Market Association figures show (in billions of dollars).</p>
<p>					    LATEST WEEK	PREVIOUS WEEK</p>
<p> PRIMARY MARKET:			   42.36		     58.48</p>
<p> OF WHICH U.S. DOLLAR ISSUES:	  20.66		     28.67</p>
<p> SECONDARY MARKET:			991.80		   1064.61</p>
<p> OF WHICH U.S. DOLLAR ISSUES:	 727.59		    796.80</p>
<p> CLEARED THROUGH EUROCLEAR	    737.91		    813.15</p>
<p> CLEARED THROUGH CEDEL		  296.25		    309.94</p>
<p>--London newsroom,  +44 171 542 7658</p>
